  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the Traditional Handcrafts Value-chain for Indigenous Women Economic Empowerment in La Guajira, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance the market competitiveness of traditional handicrafts produced by Wayuu indigenous women in the La Guajira region of Colombia by strengthening their technical capacities and improving the value chain. At the same time, it seeks to promote the social and economic empowerment of indigenous women by raising gender awareness and advancing women&apos;s rights, ultimately contributing to stable household income generation and sustainable livelihoods.&#xac00;&#xce58;&#xc0ac;&#xc2ac; &#xae30;&#xbc18; &#xad6c;&#xcd95;&#xc744; &#xd1b5;&#xd55c; &#xc6d0;&#xc8fc;&#xbbfc; &#xc5ec;&#xc131;&#xc758; &#xacbd;&#xc81c;&#xc801; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;, &#xc6d0;&#xc8fc;&#xbbfc; &#xc5ec;&#xc131;&#xc758; &#xc0ac;&#xd68c;&#xc801; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance the technical skills of Wayuu women in traditional handicraft production and improve the value chain of their crafts. In doing so, it seeks to increase household income and promote the empowerment of women through gender awareness education. The project will organize village level artisan groups and provide training in production techniques, distribution and marketing, and basic financial literacy. Furthermore, it will deliver training on gender sensitivity, human rights, and GBV prevention to strengthen women&apos;s social capacities. The initiative will be carried out in collaboration with local public vocational training centers (such as SENA) and gender focused organizations (Fuerza de Mujeres Wayuu, FMW), which will help ensure a locally adapted curriculum. Participation in trade fairs will also be facilitated to expand market access.</narrative>
  </description>
